    LLM: 'Game: Zanga. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Zanga is a Spanish trick-taking game related to Hombre/Tresillo. 4 players in 2 teams. 32-card Spanish deck. 8 each. Permanent trumps: Ace of Swords (highest), Ace of Clubs, King of Clubs. Trump chooser's team must win 5+ tricks. Winning all = bonus. Extra points for holding top 3+ trumps.",
    objective: 'The partnership that chooses trumps must win at least five of the eight tricks to score. If they take only four tricks they lose (puesta); if three or fewer they lose more (codillo). Bonuses for winning all tricks, holding the top three trumps, or winning the first five.',
    gameplay: 'Permanent trumps: A♠(Swords)=highest, A♣, K♣. Choose trump suit. Must win 5+ tricks. All 8 = bonus. Holding top 3+ trumps = extra points. Failure = puesta/codillo penalty.',
